# Rule 39 — Redesign phase PRs must include and update the phase checklist

## Why this rule exists

PRs #175–#178 ship staged implementation of the ResearchOne redesign plan
(`ResearchOne_All_Purpose_Deep_Research_Redesign_Report.md`). Reviewers and
future agents cannot verify what was done, what remains in the current phase,
or what sits in a later phase without a canonical tracking document.

## What you must do for every redesign-phase PR

### 1. Update `docs/redesign-phase-status.md` in the same commit

- Mark every item in the current phase section as `[x]` when it is fully
  implemented.
- Add new `[ ]` items for any scope discovered during implementation that is
  not in the phase definition but belongs in the same phase.
- Leave items that are **intentionally deferred** as `[ ]` under a
  "Remaining in Phase X" sub-section so readers know what ships next.
- Do **not** mark an item complete if it is only scaffolded or informational
  (e.g. "execution wired progressively" is not complete).

### 2. Include the phase status checklist in the PR description

Copy the current and next-phase sections from
`docs/redesign-phase-status.md` directly into the PR body so that the PR
diff tells the complete story without requiring a click to the file.

The PR description must contain:

```
## Redesign phase status

### Phase X — <name> (this PR)
- [x] …completed item…
- [ ] …remaining item still in Phase X…

### Phase X+1 — <name> (upcoming)
- [ ] …first item planned for next phase…
```

### 3. Pre-merge verification

Before running `report_progress` on a redesign PR:

1. `grep -n '\[ \]' docs/redesign-phase-status.md` — review every unchecked
   item and confirm it is either legitimately deferred or should be `[x]`.
2. Confirm the PR body (the description passed to `report_progress` or the
   GitHub PR body) contains the phase status block.
3. Confirm `docs/redesign-phase-status.md` is included in the staged files.

## Scope

This rule applies when:
- The branch name or commit message contains `stage-[a-z]`, `phase-[a-z]`,
  or references a redesign phase by letter.
- The PR title or body references the redesign report.
- You are asked to continue a redesign phase.

## File location

`docs/redesign-phase-status.md`
